    "updated_at": "2021-02-02T06:26:31Z",
    "body": "That's what File API does (though it's also a bit different as it doesn't have to care about letting things be read once). So the problem is not so much `bodyUsed`, but rather `ReadableStream` being accessible without side effects?\r\n\r\nBut we also use this when extracting, e.g., when constructing a `Response` from a `ReadableStream`. Why wouldn't that apply elsewhere?",
